---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import {
  ToolActivityEmpty,
  ToolActivityReceipt,
  ToolActivityRecorded,
  ToolActivityStatuses,
  ToolActivityStepper,
  ToolActivityTranscript,
  ToolActivityVariants,
} from '../../components/ToolActivityDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Tool Activity"
  description="A live timeline of the tools an agent used, with a status mark per step, web sources, and a summary that counts problems."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Tool Activity</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows the tools an agent called while it worked: what ran, what is waiting, and what needs attention.{' '}
    <code>ActivityPanel</code> frames a live run above its result.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ToolActivityStatuses client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Tools behind a reply"
      code={`import { BrandIcon } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/brand-icon";
import { ToolActivity } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/tool-activity";

<ToolActivity
  active={replyIsWorking}
  items={[
    {
      id: "call_1",
      label: "Searched the supplier inbox",
      status: "completed",
      visual: <BrandIcon brand="gmail" size="inline" />,
    },
    {
      id: "call_2",
      label: "Update the Northwind record",
      status: "failed",
      visual: <BrandIcon brand="hubspot" size="inline" />,
      detail: "The action failed. Retry, or check the app connection.",
      details: <Button variant="outline" size="sm" onClick={retry}>Retry update</Button>,
    },
  ]}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>status</code>: <code>"queued"</code>, <code>"running"</code>,<code>"waiting"</code>,{' '}
        <code>"completed"</code>,<code>"blocked"</code>, <code>"failed"</code>,<code>"cancelled"</code>, or{' '}
        <code>"unknown"</code>. Each has its own mark and a spoken name, such as “In progress” or “Outcome unknown”.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>visual</code>: a 14px icon or an inline
        <code>BrandIcon</code> for the tool or app.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>detail</code>: one short line under the label. It turns red for <code>failed</code> and{' '}
        <code>blocked</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>details</code>: extra content lined up with the label, such as a retry button or a “Details” toggle.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>active</code>: the reply is still working even when no step is running, so the trigger shows a spinner.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityVariants client:load />
    </div>
    <ul class="mt-4">
      <li>
        <code>"collapsible"</code>: the default. It opens while work is pending and closes once it settles. The trigger
        reads “Using 3 tools”, “2 tools waiting”, or “Used 3 tools · 1 needs attention”.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"transcript"</code>: starts closed under a chat reply. It reads “Working… Searching the web”, “Work
        pending”, or “Tool activity · 3 tools · Access denied”.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"stepper"</code>: always open, with no trigger. Items arrive newest first and show oldest first; inside an
        <code>ActivityPanel</code> it scrolls to the newest step.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">One tool</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityReceipt client:load />
    </div>
    <p>A single call, as on an agent request receipt. Pick a status to see its mark and how the summary changes.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In a chat reply</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityTranscript client:load />
    </div>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Transcript with web sources"
      code={`<ToolActivity
  variant="transcript"
  items={tools}
  active={isLatestTurn}
  activityLabel="Searching the web"
  onToggle={() => pauseFollowLatest()}
/>

// A web search step
{
  id: "call_7",
  label: "Searched the web",
  status: "completed",
  visual: <Globe size={14} />,
  query: "UK services inflation September 2026",
  urls: ["https://www.ons.gov.uk/…", "https://www.bls.gov/…"],
  failedUrls: ["https://www.ft.com/…"],
  sources: [{ url: "https://www.ons.gov.uk/…", title: "Consumer price inflation, UK" }],
}`}
    />
    <p>
      Web steps show their search text and up to four source chips; a “2 more” button shows the rest. A page in{' '}
      <code>failedUrls</code>
      gets a warning icon. Chips without a title show the address without
      <code>https://www.</code>. Only <code>http</code> and
      <code>https</code> addresses become links, which open in a new tab.
    </p>
    <p>
      Source chips are <a href="/components/web-source/">Web Source</a> chips, so they show each site's favicon. Pass
      <code>sourceIcon</code> to use another icon service; it returns an image address for a page, or nothing for a
      globe.
    </p>
    <p>
      With no items, an <code>active</code> transcript shows “Thinking…” or the <code>activityLabel</code>. Other
      variants render nothing.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Activity panel</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityStepper client:load />
    </div>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A live run above its result"
      code={`import { ActivityPanel, ToolActivity } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/tool-activity";

<ActivityPanel working={running} activityLabel={currentStep} hasResult collapseWhenDone>
  <ToolActivity
    variant="stepper"
    items={steps}
    hasOlder={page.hasMore}
    loadingOlder={page.loading}
    olderError={page.failed}
    onLoadOlder={page.loadMore}
    onRetryOlder={page.loadMore}
  />
</ActivityPanel>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        The panel takes at most 40% of its parent’s height and scrolls inside. A soft fade covers the top once it
        scrolls.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>hasResult</code> draws a line under the panel.
        <code>collapseWhenDone</code> closes it when work stops and reopens it when work restarts.
      </li>
      <li>
        When <code>hasOlder</code> is set, scrolling within 40px of the top calls
        <code>onLoadOlder</code> once. While
        <code>loadingOlder</code> it says “Loading earlier activity…”; on
        <code>olderError</code> it shows “Retry loading”.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Recorded activity</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityRecorded client:load />
    </div>
    <p>
      A finished run can sit behind a <code>ResultCard</code>. Its details show the stepper without a panel.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Empty</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ToolActivityEmpty client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger is a button named by its summary, and the summary is a live <code>status</code>. Steps are an ordered
      list named “Tool activity” (set <code>label</code> to rename it). Each step says its status, such as “Failed”; a
      running step’s status is announced outside the transcript. Source chips sit in a list named “Web sources”, and
      failed pages say “Page unavailable”.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ActivityPanel</code> is a region named “Chat activity”. Its timeline is a focusable region named “Activity
      timeline”, so it scrolls by keyboard. Older-load errors are an <code>alert</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Steps fade in over 180ms and the chevron turns in 120ms. With reduced motion, steps appear at once and running
      marks stop spinning. On touch screens the trigger and source chips grow to 44px.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Rows use <code>--sprout-text</code> and <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Marks use <code>--sprout-success</code>{' '}
      (running),
      <code>--sprout-primary</code> (completed), <code>--sprout-info</code>
      (waiting), and <code>--sprout-danger</code>. Chips use
      <code>--sprout-secondary</code> and <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Set
      <code>--sprout-activity-panel-fade</code> to the panel’s background when it is not <code>--sprout-surface</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
